68: 4. **B4 fair alternatives:** the same margin and lower-limit rule against every other arm.
69: 5. **B5 retention:** the Phase A development set, scored again after Phase B, falls by at most 10% of its Phase A score.
70: 6. **B6 audit:** independent replay confirms every feedback event, certificate, file hash, unchanged-memory check, zero input collisions and zero exact repeats.
71: 
72: **Stopping rules:**
73: 
74: 1. Do not start unless Phase A passed all six section 9 rules, the checker and generator passed audit, and the input check found zero collisions.
75: 2. Training stops at exactly 480 trials. The snapshot is the checkpoint with the most correct development pairs; a tie goes to the earliest. If any single development count is lower than at the previous checkpoint by more than 10%, that checkpoint cannot be chosen.
76: 3. A run stops early only for a failed safety check before training starts, a failed audit or a software fault. It is reported and repeated in a new run folder with the same numbers. A fault after the locked set is opened spends that set.
77: 4. The locked set is opened once. No limit is lowered and no new try uses the same set.
78: 
111: 
112: **Locked problems:** 60 twin pairs from 60 unrelated games. Every board is a capture that would lose material if recaptured, and a pinned enemy piece attacks the target square.
113: 
114: - 30 **pin pairs:** the only attacker of the target is pinned (good) or the pin line is blocked so it is not pinned (bad).
115: - 30 **recapture pairs:** the pinned attacker is present on both twins; an extra unpinned attacker is absent (good) or present (bad).
116: 
117: **Practice:** 480 trials of idea 1 and 480 trials of idea 2 [choice]. Order is idea 1 then 2 in run 1, idea 2 then 1 in run 2, and alternating blocks of 96 in run 3.
118: 
119: **Arms:** Full fly (ideas 1 and 2); idea-1-only fly (480 filler trials in place of idea 2); idea-2-only fly (filler in place of idea 1); fresh fly (960 filler trials); shuffled-feedback fly; plasticity-off fly; simple learner; similar-board recall; exact-recall store; and the **fixed-sum combiner**, which adds the idea-1-only fly's and idea-2-only fly's move scores with a fixed rule. The fixed-sum combiner tests the review's warning that a hand-written rule could combine two answers without the fly learning to combine.
120: 
121: **Pass scores (all three runs):**
122: 
123: 1. **C1-a:** Full fly at least 44/60.
124: 2. **C1-b:** at least 22/30 on pin pairs and at least 22/30 on recapture pairs.
125: 3. **C1-c:** at least 6 more pairs than every other arm, including the best single-idea fly and the fixed-sum combiner, each with bootstrap lower limit above 0.
126: 4. **C1-d:** retention: each single idea's development set falls by at most 10%.
127: 5. **C1-e:** independent audit, as B6.
128: 
129: **Before C1 runs:** a software check on made-up data must show that the frozen move score can express all four required answer patterns (both idea conditions on and off) without a selector. If it cannot, stop and report it as a limit of the score, not a failure of the fly.
130: 
131: ### C2: ideas 1, 2 and 3
132: 
133: **Locked problems:** 60 twin pairs from 60 unrelated games. Every board is a capture where a pinned enemy piece attacks the target square and the exchange value matters.
134: 
135: - 20 **pin pairs:** captured value lower than the capturing piece; the only attacker is pinned (good) or not pinned (bad).
136: - 20 **recapture pairs:** captured value lower; the pinned attacker is on both twins; an unpinned attacker is absent (good) or present (bad).
137: - 20 **value pairs:** an unpinned attacker is on both twins; the captured piece is worth at least the capturing piece (good) or less (bad).
138: 
139: **Practice:** 480 trials of each idea [choice], with three counterbalanced orders across the three runs (1-2-3, 3-1-2, and alternating blocks of 96).
140: 
141: **Arms:** Full fly; each two-idea fly (filler in place of the missing idea); each single-idea fly; fresh fly; shuffled-feedback fly; plasticity-off fly; simple learner; similar-board recall; exact-recall store; fixed-sum combiner of the three single-idea flies.
142: 
143: **Pass scores (all three runs):**
144: 
145: 1. **C2-a:** Full fly at least 44/60.
146: 2. **C2-b:** at least 15/20 on each of the three pair groups. (At random, the chance for one group is 2.1%.)
147: 3. **C2-c:** at least 6 more pairs than every other arm, including the best two-idea fly and the fixed-sum combiner, each with bootstrap lower limit above 0.

