- **RESOLVED — Normal draws.** The formula, draw order, discarded partner, and matrix fill order are fixed. [Design:207](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:207)
- **RESOLVED — Case-recall stores.** The diary lookup uses the frozen diary, the full-history lookup stores one entry per original lesson, and only the simple learners update on replays. [Design:282](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:282), [design:349](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:349)

**New findings**

1. **required-BUILD — The matched tape admits events the learner cannot apply.** The tape permits an event with no teaching input and requires an update for every event, but the update needs a pulse sign. Implementations could reject the same tape or train differently. Require a pulse on every lesson and replay row, and keep no-pulse trials out of the tape, consistent with the existing lesson rule. [Design:183](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:183), [design:284](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:284), [design:349](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:349)
2. **required-LAUNCH — The known-answer check lacks an independent reference.** Stage 0 says to publish eight values per seed without specifying how the expected values are obtained. A generator can reproduce its own error. Freeze independently computed reference values and specify the comparison tolerance before running the check. [Design:207](/C:/Users/ethan/Documents/fly-chess-research/documentation/design/neural-learning/replay-diary-memory-design-2026-11-17.md:207)
